      },
      "worked": "Independence gives\n$$P(A\\cap B)=P(A)\\times P(B).$$\nMutual exclusivity gives\n$$P(A\\cap B)=0.$$\nTherefore,\n$$P(A)\\times P(B)=0.$$\nA product is zero only if at least one factor is zero. Hence $P(A)=0$ or $P(B)=0$.",
